{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul","id":1191027,"title":"Advice on tasks and chores for a PC ghoul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T10:03:27-08:00","id":1191027,"title":"Advice on tasks and chores for a PC ghoul","content":"So I've been playing a CofD chronicle for a while now, and the players have starting making some friends, allies and foes between the different splats etc etc. One of my players has recently become a Ghoul to a young Daeva neonate that is quite childish and outgoing, a party-going drug-and-sex-addict that belongs in the Circle of the Crone. For now She treats the PC &quot;quite well&quot; as her new boyfriend (and she probably sees it that way), giving him an ample blood supply, drugging him before she eats a bit, going to clubs and having a &quot;good time&quot; for the most part. She's started to ask him for a few favors like picking up some new clothes, getting some cocaine and doing some laundry, even ask for help with a fucked up feeding-frenzy gone wrong so he had to clean it up.<br /> Shes part of a coterie that with only CoC members that focus on carnal desire through sex, drugs &amp; rock n' roll basically.<br /> <br /> He's met the rest and even got a brief interview with the Keeper of Elysium so that he can become a registered ghoul. In this city, which is controlled by a Carthian Senate, ghouls have some decent respect and more then a few priviliges compared to your standard first ed. invictus city. The registred ghouls are considered members of the City and may even buy City and Covenant Status and join a Covenant, though it\u2019s still limited to one, and most laws and rights appliyng to Kindred is also applied to Ghouls. They even have voting rights on the elections of the city. <br /> <br /> But here\u2019s my problem, I have not played a Ghoul chronicle before, well not since the old V:tM days anyway where ghouls usually wasn\u2019t treated any better then gimp-suited slave-furniture. As well as in most chronicles I\u2019ve played in Vampire (both sorts) ghouls haven\u2019t really been very important but I really want to change both my own and my players veiws on ghouls, making them into persons so to speak, givning them character. I\u2019ve got a few ghoul NPCs that stand out with much more focus then before so there I think im gonna be quite happy. But.<br /> I\u2019ve read both half-damned and the old ghoul-book but it doesn\u2019t really give me much advice on practical matters ghouls can be asked to do on a daily basis. It only talks in abstract terms about service and stuff. I need help to finding out what the regnant could be asking the ghoul on a daily/nightly basis. More appreciated is \u2019normal\u2019 stuff as in laundry and repairs and such then supernatural things so to speak.<br /> <br /> And last a bit about the PC, he\u2019s damaged goods, super low Integrity, a bit Condition-heavy (usually), muscle-man thug more then brains and a manly-macho-man and works as a bouncer on a respected and hard to get into nightclub. He was once a half-famous boxer but now is an has-been that got suspended. He\u2019s pretty well in most physical aspects and can keep up in social encounters. As well he has a dot in Majesty and two in Vigor by now, and is probably gonna buy the Beast Whisperer merit that allow him to talk down vampires from frenzy.<br /> <br /> So please give me some ideas about what the Vampire can as of her PC ghoul?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T10:45:09-08:00","id":1191037,"title":"","content":"(Disclaimer: Not a Vampire expert)<br /> <br /> Since Ghouls can operate in the day:<ul><li>They can maintain the Haven, in that &quot;yes, someone lives here&quot;.<ul><li>Talk to neighbors.</li> <li>Been seen on the property.</li> <li>Be available to answer the door - such as for police, etc.</li> </ul></li> <li>They can conduct business where requiring only contact at night would be suspicious or difficult. Banks, and government facilities, don't hold hours conductive to vampires.<ul><li>Someone has to be filed as the owner, and it is a good idea if they can appear when needed.</li> <li>Majesty is nice and all, but having a valid drivers license and other paperwork is helpful.</li> </ul></li> <li>Since other Kindred are asleep, Ghouls can work without their interference, in case you need spying done, or another vampire wacked (I don't know the rules regarding inter-Kindred violence in that Domain, though).</li> </ul>Basically, having a Ghoul can provided the necessary cover for the Masquerade. Remembering that in 2E it isn't so much &quot;vampires don't exist&quot; but more &quot;[Person in question] isn't a vampire&quot;.<br /> <br /> And besides the kind of daily tasks that only day-walking Ghouls can do? Nearly anything. You said she's a party animal? Doesn't sound like she wants to spend the time on &quot;trivial&quot; things, like cleaning, the above paperwork, etc.<br /> <br /> Just remember that your Ghoul is human too, and needs time for their own chores, as well as food and sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T11:20:26-08:00","id":1191057,"title":"","content":"Anything she doesn't want to do herself is the real answer. Find out the background on that new graffiti tag, pick up drugs (unless she want's to keep his record clean), clean the haven or bring in some cash.<br /> On top of that he has to remember that he's a boyfriend and is expected to be able to take her on dates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:36:09-08:00","id":1191083,"title":"","content":"Change the oil in her car(s). <br /> Get the car(s) tuned up.<br /> Mow the lawn. <br /> Take the (animal) pet(s) to the vet. <br /> Clean the gutters.<br /> Shingle the roof.<br /> Act as a bodyguard for her blood dolls.<br /> <br /> Since the regnant is an overt degenerate, she could pimp him out for sex, leg breaker services for loan sharking and drug dealing. Or have him do mundane chores for her coterie members and &quot;friends&quot; in exchange for favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-02-2018, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:26:34-08:00","id":1191126,"title":"","content":"Find Poacher's so that master may &quot;Deal with&quot; them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T09:49:11-07:00","id":1198012,"title":"","content":"A little late, but thanks for the input and ideas. Just more normal stuff, it got me some good ideas and new ones keep on popping up now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T11:41:54-07:00","id":1198050,"title":"","content":"Glad to help, is the player enjoying it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T11:49:56-07:00","id":1198057,"title":"","content":"I've only got as far as to implement a few of the ideas, a grievous leg wound sent as a warning for messing with a Seer has put some of his ghoul responsibilities on halt as they have enlisted another ghoul npc to sneak him out of the hospital and to have his regnant trying to get enough blood to help him heal it. Though that has helped with us going into more of a personal approach of what the relationship looks like and looking into the relationship between ghouls and such. As soon's he's better we'll look into more of the day to day life and chores a bit more. So far, he (and the rest) enjoys this as it gives them a far better look on the ins and outs of being a ghoul, in contrast to see it from a vampires perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T00:55:33-07:00","id":1198579,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being Normal&quot; (ie maintaining a facade of likable banality and normalcy) while secretly housing a vampire offers a vampire many benefits. That isn't going to be the ghoul doing the errand running, maintaining a life which looks normal is a full time job and can easily be ruined by errands that involve anything supernatural. But shifting which ghoul does that if the current ghoul's card is turned over is the three card monte that clever vampires play with their haven (<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/KansasCityShuffle\" target=\"_blank\">Kansas shuffle</a>, tip if he's smart, <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0428.html\" target=\"_blank\">he isn't at any of the options presented in the first place</a>) <br /> <br /> From what I read of how this ghoul is being used and exposed to danger so far, if a ghoul who manages a haven, it is best as one of the decoy homes. Also that would make sense why he suffered retribution. <br /> <br /> As for mundane tasks for a ghoul exposed to moderate to high risk, secure message courier is a great one. Picking up and dropping of messages at drop offs in times and places difficult for vampires to intercept, like in the middle of the day is a public venue with a police presence. Some message may be packages, some letters, others are verbal only where they must meet someone else's pawn and exchange prearranged pass phrases and responses to identify each other. The chance of being followed, being intercepted, manipulated, and all other types of intrigue are possible down this route, make the vampire's higher level of intrigue possible. <br /> <br /> You could flip the script and instead have the ghoul try to break into someone else secure line of communication about, intercept messages, follow messagers home so you can report where they are.<br /> <br /> Since the vampire is having a issue with the Seer and this pawn is already exposed, the vampire if wise would want to avoid using that pawn against the Seer unless it was needed for the master stroke coup de grace checkmate, most likely lethal or worse for the Seer, perhaps by using the ghoul in such the way the Seer tries to strike again and finds themselves very dead in a trap instead, ei the ghoul will be used to antagonize the Seer in such a way as to be the bait of a trap separate from the ghouls own mechanization (because the ghoul is exposed and you must assume is constantly watched) so likely the nature of those mechanization which are an invisible safety net during the trap will almost certainly be unknown to the ghoul. In fact since the ghoul has been attacked that means almost certainly if anything goes wrong from the Seers point of view they blame the vampire and then predictable try the punish the vampire by striking at the ghoul again, this time more viciously and thus extend themselves so that the Seer could be caught. If the vampire is REALLY wise he won't even be in the safety net trap against the Seer, it'll be unrelated forces he got to move in that direct by manipulate a fourth or fifth removed parties whom themselves are working via proxy twice over. Vampires are very capable of weaving some crazy twisted webs of plots and counter plots..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T05:13:41-07:00","id":1198613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1198579#post1198579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Being Normal&quot; (ie maintaining a facade of likable banality and normalcy) while secretly housing a vampire offers a vampire many benefits. That isn't going to be the ghoul doing the errand running, maintaining a life which looks normal is a full time job and can easily be ruined by errands that involve anything supernatural. But shifting which ghoul does that if the current ghoul's card is turned over is the three card monte that clever vampires play with their haven (<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/KansasCityShuffle\" target=\"_blank\">Kansas shuffle</a>, tip if he's smart, <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0428.html\" target=\"_blank\">he isn't at any of the options presented in the first place</a>)<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah keeping another decoy haven for the vampire is probably a good idea. The coteries' domain/feeding ground is pretty much besieged by revenants and the neighboring coteries. Or well besieged is a harsh word, but there are some border friction at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for mundane tasks for a ghoul exposed to moderate to high risk, secure message courier is a great one. Picking up and dropping of messages at drop offs in times and places difficult for vampires to intercept, like in the middle of the day is a public venue with a police presence. Some message may be packages, some letters, others are verbal only where they must meet someone else's pawn and exchange prearranged pass phrases and responses to identify each other. The chance of being followed, being intercepted, manipulated, and all other types of intrigue are possible down this route, make the vampire's higher level of intrigue possible. </div> </div> </div>Courier is a pretty interesting job with lots of possibilities for fun things to happen and meeting up with more ghouls, servants and just other people connected to the vampire(s) over all etc. Will probably use this. Perhaps using him to get something important delivered to a specialized coterie of couriers that's in the city, introducing them for later use...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the vampire is having a issue with the Seer and this pawn is already exposed &lt;more text&gt; </div> </div> </div>This is more a personal vendetta from the ghoul PC and not from the vampire or the Seer. The Seer NPC in question is a Douche grand master laissez faire capitalist brat that the PC (and player) really hates for throwing money around like a complete dick and treating all people like commodities to be bought. So in a desperate move when the fire alarm went off in a club, the PC jabbed the Seer in the back, almost killing him, and the seers Pylon-mate threw the PC into twilight for the rest of the scene, and later shot him in the knee as a (final) warning. To be fair against the Player and the PC, they had no idea that he or his friends was Seers or mages at all.<br /> So far he's been lying to his regnant about them being some form of supernaturals, instead saying he got mugged bad from some shit dude that got rejected from the club he's working at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:37:13-07:00","id":1198799,"title":"","content":"A revenant problem, you say? Do they have rights too or is this exactly the sort of problem best solved by someone diurnal making them disappear? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:08:04-07:00","id":1198815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1198799#post1198799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A revenant problem, you say? Do they have rights too or is this exactly the sort of problem best solved by someone diurnal making them disappear? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yeah, kinda, not in their own right, but some of them manage to &quot;behave&quot; and become accepted into kindred society, if only on the lower levels. Most of them however are considered more of a pest problem, that yes, surely is a thing best solved by someone active when they sleep. (Thanks for a new awesome word i didn't know as well. Diurnal...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T02:59:52-07:00","id":1198988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1198613#post1198613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more a personal vendetta from the ghoul PC and not from the vampire or the Seer. The Seer NPC in question is a Douche grand master laissez faire capitalist brat that the PC (and player) really hates for throwing money around like a complete dick and treating all people like commodities to be bought. So in a desperate move when the fire alarm went off in a club, the PC jabbed the Seer in the back, almost killing him, and the seers Pylon-mate threw the PC into twilight for the rest of the scene, and later shot him in the knee as a (final) warning. To be fair against the Player and the PC, they had no idea that he or his friends was Seers or mages at all.<br /> So far he's been lying to his regnant about them being some form of supernaturals, instead saying he got mugged bad from some shit dude that got rejected from the club he's working at.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VideoGameCrueltyPotential\" target=\"_blank\">Wow! Stabbed a guy that he didn't really know too personally in the back at a nightclub for being a pompous and unlikable?</a> That PC is either a Psychopath or a Sociopath. Especially since he's a glib enough liar to fool a vampire. He'll not change much after an embrace I fear, devouring other people is metaphorically business as usual for someone like that, except if he's going to live long he needs to learn impulse control, and how to play the long game.<br /> <br /> So even though the vampire doesn't know about the Mage i'd expect the mage to shortly find out about the vampire. I mean the seer must investigate into the ghoul because the ghoul could likely be a pawn of another Seer Plylon trying to make a move against the Seer and his Pylon. (For non-Mage players Seers of the Throne are the Mages with the most Vampire like in puppetteering politics and backstabbing of the types of mages). Shooting the ghoul in the knee was brilliant for the blood splatter for sympathetic scrying later, as is leaving him alive so the Seer can use that scrying to follow him back to whatever master is influencing him, and when he see's it's a Vampire, unless the Seers Pylon does a deep mind probe on the Vampire and comes back satisfied with the lack of evidence that it was on purpose, I can't imagine the Seer's cabal presuming nothing scheme-y nor nefarious. (it is possible they are satisfied by a mental probe, maybe not too, but if there is no mental probe they must assume it was at the orders of the Vampire, just to play it safe) Also I presume this isn't the first time something like this has happened between the local Seers, and they likely have non-aggression agreements with Vampire leadership which they both brokered through pawns, now the Seers bring this infraction to light and the Regnant of the PC is the one accountable in vampire society, and ghouls are viewed as property, so odds are in a bit through Seer and Vampire politics the ghoul will be liquidated as a liability with their master, given as a gift to the Seers with a tithe of Vitae to keep it a ghoul from the PC's staked regnant serving a term of punishment in that condition and used as a Vitae machine by the local Vampires, or the seen as redeemable and given to a new Regnant while their old master suffers whatever punishment was deemed appropriate. In short that ghoul really ruined things for their master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-24-2018, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T04:44:13-07:00","id":1199004,"title":"","content":"Or, if the Seer was Scrying right when the Ghoul lied to their Regnant and covered up the incident... Instant blackmail material. &quot;You do these things for me, and I won't out what really happened to your Vampire or cause an incident.&quot; Why admit to weakness just for some petty diplomatic vengence when you can get a pawn with atypical abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T05:11:13-07:00","id":1199007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot