plete dick and treating all people like commodities to be bought&quot;</u> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DisproportionateRetribution\" target=\"_blank\">attempting to stab them to death</a> is a hallmark of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSociopath\" target=\"_blank\">a sociopath who things they won't get penalized for the action</a> or a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheUnfettered\" target=\"_blank\">psychopath who doesn't care if it is detrimental to their own well-being</a>. Hey, I get it people undervalue the severeness and seriousness of violence in games and react as if inflict death on other people was something which was normal to most people, it isn't and studies do show it is psychologically damaging, and even most people in prison aren't even murderers, and even current modern soldiers who've have the opportunity to exchange fire in active, which by the way are a minority, don't have confirmed kills and shot in the hopes to suppress fire of the enemy. Kind of a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IJustWantToBeBadass\" target=\"_blank\">buzz kill </a>to the violence <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PowerFantasy\" target=\"_blank\">power fantasy</a>, but that's reality. Now for Drama we have more artistic licence, but for a character to remain &quot;good&quot; they must be given serious and meaningful motivations, like other people in real danger, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AcceptableBreaksFromReality\" target=\"_blank\">having been push far enough so the audience feels it's justified</a>. I mean if we watched a show with a 10 year old called names by a 12 year old and then the 12 year old spat on the 10 year old's friend, followed immediately by the 10 year old stabbing the 12 year old with severe over killing with a butcher knife until the whole scene was covered in blood most of us would would realize that the 10 year old was the crazy and dangerous one and the 12 year old was just a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AssholeVictim\" target=\"_blank\">jerk victim</a> of the real monster, the 10 year old.<br /> <br /> In short the PC is as much of a monster as a standard vampire or Seer, more monstrous than a humane vampire, which is a bit ironic in the case of humane vampires see a human is less bothered by killing other humans than they are about killing humans, in the light the vampire is an udead copse that feeds on blood being less of a monster than a living human who has no supernatural drive to kill or victim humans. All that said, not unusual for a vampire whom may have ghouled someone useful whom also the embrace and horrible there after will not be too traumatic, in case the ghoul/regnant relationship developed into a childe/sire one..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-24-2018, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:54:32-07:00","id":1199056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199034#post1199034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underlined actual motivation listed.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know that's why the PC hates the NPC, but we don't know that that's the actual immediate cause of violence breaking out. Like, they mentioned a fire alarm, but not why that went off; so there's clearly more going on that they cut for brevity. My point is it might have made more sense in the actual game, and we shouldn't jump to conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:18:32-07:00","id":1199065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199007#post1199007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Good point and if the scrying happen to catch that exact moment then additionally it proves the vampire wasn't the threat, a natural presumption if their isn't meaningful and substantial evidence to the contrary. If the scrying isn't &quot;recording&quot; for continual coverage that can be reviewed or guided via Fate or Time a bit of a lucky find. Totally possible, depending on the Pylon's communal expertise, to have either of those types of scrying, but not assured as the make up of the Pylon is not shared via this thread yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering this a story, rather than calculated probability, they don't even need Fate or Time, if the Storyteller is willing. They could have started Scrying as soon as they acquired the blood. Track the assailant back to their control and find out they were acting on their own, and <i>lied</i> about it. Instead of worrying about a continued assault on their persons, now they have a potential undetected pawn and spy amongst vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199007#post1199007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the presumption the vampire acted on purpose through a ghoul, it isn't petty vengence but a statement to vampire Leadership to keep a tight reign on their lessers and crack down, which both maintains stability and oppression, things Seers really like. Domination and displays of political strength are real things which if you are in a position of power through, you may find yourself under attack if you slip at maintaining them, ei there is no weakness in admitting a vampire failed to successfully attack you (the vampire, not the ghoul, the ghoul isn't a person but an object owned by the vampire who is responsible for its every action in the eyes of two terrible tyrannical group of monsters, Vampire Society and Seers of the Throne) and demanding the vampire to be punished as an object lesson. The ghoul is and will likely remain property, either of the vampire, another vampire, or a Seer and if not they are most likely dead which doesn't prevent petty Seers with Death from enjoying a new ghost servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presumes certain things about both factions that I'm not comfortable extrapolating without more information. As stated in the OP, the Ghoul is considered a Citizen of the Carthian ruled Domain, so they already aren't mere &quot;property&quot; to be forfeited via proxy. We know nothing of the Seer organization in the area, nor what political treaties, if any, they have with the vampires. They might be the only Pylon in the area, or new, and so don't have any great political heft other that what they can personally enforce.<br /> <br /> And which makes for a better story &quot;You now have to balance obligations to different masters due to your actions&quot; or &quot;you are screwed for consequences you had no real way of knowing - kiss goodbye to that character concept&quot;? One is workable within the existing game (and leads to more plot hooks), and the other dumps the character or requires a drastic change in concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199007#post1199007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funniest/Cruelest version? The Seer did see the lie, knows the truth the vampire is innocent, both black mails the ghoul to get a few favors and then demand punishment of the ghouls regent anyway, and asking for the ghoul as a slave as compensation treating then get the ghoul all 'Stockholmed' with alternating abuse and kindness into an obedient pet.<br /> <br /> The only funnier thing would the Ghoul then Awakening, and then being initiated as a Seer of the Throne, all in earnest because, that's the type of cut-throat power starved person the PC is at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, again, torpedoes the character, and would require in-depth crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-24-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:44:40-07:00","id":1199092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199065#post1199065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This presumes certain things about both factions that I'm not comfortable extrapolating without more information.</div> </div> </div> </div>True and valid point. But with rights come accountability and that's a bit worse for the ghoul because then they become responsible for their own actions and if a head in needed on a pike they it well could be their own, and they lack the benefit of being able to be staked as a vampiric form of imprisonment so as far as punishment goes that is... limiting in how they can be dealt with in a serious Attempted murder charge. If you can't really lock someone away as a punishment and they are lethally and politically dangerous that's why people get executed. We also don't know what kind of deals Carthians have made with the other supernaturals of the city. For example my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=990642#post990642\">Carthians Set in the city of Portland Oregon</a> are 100% in bed with the Seers to the point it is an outright alliance to keep the Pentacle off the vampire's back so that'd be a major faux paux (the Pentacle Consilium has a non-aggression policy against the local vampires for this reason which is explained to young Mages to avoid trouble). And unless the city is lacking in Mysteries, which it isn't because we know it has Seers, or has a Pentacle so strong the Seers are the underdogs, which is not the standard in canon, Seers are going to be a big deal, and likely heavy hitters, especially in cities large enough to house complex vampire population like we are discussing. Which is how I came to my extrapolation, but hey, maybe we're talking about even more extreme outlier than merely a city ruled by Carthians that give ghouls the same rights as young Kindred, and I am way off base, as I am just playing the odds with my ideas in the lack of more information.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1199056#post1199056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know that's why the PC hates the NPC, but we don't know that that's the actual immediate cause of violence breaking out. Like, they mentioned a fire alarm, but not why that went off; so there's clearly more going on that they cut for brevity. My point is it might have made more sense in the actual game, and we shouldn't jump to conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true, though if there was a better reason for attempting to kill the person whom turned out to be a Seer I think it worth more mentioning than the purple prose on the PC and Player's disgust at the type of person the NPC was,which was the focus of what was presented. A bit like like trying to watch a play through a a muffled key peephole I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-24-2018, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:08:49-07:00","id":1199473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1191027-advice-on-tasks-and-chores-for-a-pc-ghoul?p=1198988#post1198988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VideoGameCrueltyPotential\" target=\"_blank\">Wow! Stabbed a guy that he didn't really know too personally in the back at a nightclub for being a pompous and unlikable?</a> That PC is either a Psychopath or a Sociopath. Especially since he's a glib enough liar to fool a vampire. He'll not change much after an embrace I fear, devouring other people is metaphorically business as usual for someone like that, except if he's going to live long he needs to learn impulse control, and how to play the long game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well short answer, there was a bit more then met the eye about the attack. The Seer, was acting out as a complete shitbag and deserved to get a punch in the back, some new Vigor that the PC didn't grasp the fullest understanding of and some real (un)luck with the dice was turned a &quot;semi-harmless&quot; situation into an assault with almost deadly consequence. Lying to his regnant was out of fear of her safety, he didn't want to drag her into it. Not realizing the full potential problem, and to be fair, why would he. But surely, im not arguing that the PCs in this chronicle are pretty broken and really FUBAR all of them, but that's been because of everything they been through, which a year later in play, is a fair bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> shooting the ghoul in the knee was brilliant for the blood splatter for sympathetic scrying later, as is leaving him alive so the Seer can use that scrying </div> </div> </div>This was pretty much what happened. Also a bit later, the Seer used that information to black-mail the ghoul into cooperating with him. Knowing of he's lack of care of others health, he's organizing the PC for a hit against an enemy. <br /> <br /> As for the Vampire/Mage relations in the city. There's a cooperating non-aggression pact between the factions, both are to not interfere with the others and not spill blood, both eager to keep lids on the masquerade/veil to keep normies from knowing to much about the occult happenings in the city. The Seer pylon, which there's only a small Mammon pylon in the city is deep inside the fashion and advertisement scene and are members in the Consilium of the city which is mostly ruled by Guardians. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:43:12-07:00","id":1199480,"title":"","content":"Not responding to anyone in particular and not defending the actions of the player or the PC, more trying to explain a bit of the circumstance.<br /> <br /> Some of the reasons the fight started (short on why it escalated is in the above post) was because the Seer, knowing that the PC was a sleepwalker but not yet what kind and wanted to expose him and embarrass him in front of the other guests and clients of the club in where the PC is a host/bouncer. The Seer showed up before they opened, demanded that they opened for him and his entourage, bribing them, ordered a lot of expensive drinks and spoiled them (vaskade) down the drain <a href=\"https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Vaska\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Vaska</a> , threw shit around, groped the waitresses and coworkers to the PC, over-all insulted people and showered bystanders with champagne among and bribed the police to leave them alone among other things. So in short, not really knowing in-charachter how Vigor yet worked (really new ghoul, and a regnant not really that informative on the whole vampire-business things yet) and lot's of 10-again got what would be just a fuck you punch in the back into almost killing the &quot;poor&quot; seer.<br /> <br /> As for the relations of the city's vamps and mages and such, as above again.<br /> Let's start, the domain in ruled by a carthian senate, that makes the laws and appoint the prince for a five year mandate to uphold the law and secure the food supply, e.g. seeing that vamps are allowed their feeding grounds and such, the people vote on most appointments of other officers for the domain and the ghouls are emancipated and giving votes in the elections. In that regard the ghouls are not only considered property but as a lower class of citizens and people in their own right among their fellow kindred citizens. However, if a crime happens by the hand of a ghoul, the regnant is considered a co-conspirator of the crime, but only if the regnant was informed of what happened (although unbeknownst to the PCs and the players) .<br /> <br /> The mages in the domain has reconstructed a new Consilium in the last decades after a long war between the mages and forsaken of the area, both splats was almost extinct in the area before the archmaster in the city intervened and put up a large protection spell around the city from the werewolves, creating a barrier in the shadow that can't be crossed and any werewolf that changes inside or enters the shadow is in all simplicity killed by the spell. This has created a new sub-ecosystem of the local shadow almost fully encapsulated from the rest which is the single one mystery of the new conslium to explore, in where they now have laws to be really careful around the shadow and the now gone archmasters protective spells. Given the last decades of almost open warfare and after with the spirits of the city living in their own ecosystem, there is a lot, a lot, of occult phenomena in the city so the guardians are really keen on trying to keep the lid on the occult, in that the sought out allies in the city, lowering their weapons and making an unholy alliance with the seer pylon and local kindred to keep the normies as unknowing of the darkness as could be.<br /> The mages though consider themselves the ultimate authority among inferiors and have excessive use of closed tribunals for their legislative system, passing the leadership around every few years to avoid tyranny.<br /> Most of the alliance is about the &quot;nocturnal states&quot; to help each others enforce public knowledge and opinion away from the occult and breeches of the veil/masquerade and to stay out of each others business. Although a fair bit of information-trading and schemes and plots roll over to each other on an individual basis, most they stay out of sight from each other. There are ambassadors that try to mediate and come to understandings in conflict interests between the parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}